  "what": "Tane, alone at a dead end, fights off flying security drones (the drones are NOT in the drawings); in every one of these drawings he holds a pipe in his RIGHT hand. The PIPE: a plain straight length of pale steel-grey water pipe about as long as his arm (90 cm) and as thick as his wrist, with one darker threaded coupling ring at its far end; it is exactly the same pipe in every drawing that has it. Drawing 1 (seen from in front and from below): the CATCH: his LEFT arm is thrown straight up above his head, its fist clenched tight as if it has just grabbed a thick handle out of the air (the fist is EMPTY: a closed fist with nothing in it), his head tipped back looking up at that fist, grinning with his teeth; the pipe hangs low in his RIGHT hand; feet braced wide. Drawing 2 (he faces the viewer's RIGHT): he holds his LEFT (far) arm straight out in front of him at shoulder height, fist clenched as if holding something heavy at arm's length by a handle (EMPTY fist), leaning back a little against its weight, looking past the fist with one eyebrow raised and a slow grin; the pipe low at his side in his RIGHT (near) hand. Drawing 3 (facing RIGHT): the COIL: the LEFT fist drawn right back up behind his head like a pitcher about to throw (EMPTY clenched fist), body arched back and twisted, weight on the back leg; the pipe in his RIGHT hand out low in front for balance; eyes locked forward to the right, teeth bared. Drawing 4 (facing RIGHT): the SLAM: a huge overarm throw-down at full stretch: he lunges forward onto his deeply bent front leg, the LEFT arm whipped down and forward, straight, its EMPTY clenched fist low out in front of him at knee height, his chest thrown down over the front knee, the RIGHT arm with the pipe flung straight out behind him, the back leg stretched out behind, the coat flying up behind; a ferocious delighted grin. Drawing 5 (front three-quarter view): straightening up out of the lunge, breathing out, shoulders dropping, the pipe swinging up loosely in his RIGHT hand, left hand relaxed, a crooked satisfied smile. Drawing 6 (front three-quarter view): the winner: standing tall and easy, weight on one leg, the pipe resting across his RIGHT shoulder, held by its end in his right hand, his LEFT fist on his hip, chin up, the widest grin showing his teeth; the coat hangs still.",
